# quality-mgr, 2026-09-06, qa-phase-aw-integration-review-r2: also confirmed
# FIXED, but neither of these ever had a triage:hasOccurrence link to the
# finding (they were narrative-only citations), so no in-place occurrence
# edit is needed for the branch-scoped gate -- recorded here for completeness
# only. (2) duplicate truncate_utf8/truncate_detail -> single truncate_detail
# impl only (diagnostic_timeline.rs:177-190), via 6812ac631; (3) dangling
# lint_rules id -> "peer-dial-seam" resolves to a real registered task
# (.just/lint_peer_dial_seam.py, wired in .just/run_lint.py:57,193-194),
# already closed in an earlier round (see fix-aw-readiness-easy-d9fa67fcc-c9
# below); (8) admission-layer bypass on /v1/health and /v1/diagnostics ->
# with_auxiliary_admission wraps both behind the same
# LoadShedLayer+ConcurrencyLimitLayer+HandleErrorLayer stack (lib.rs:580-635),
# citing "AW-READY-O7 items C12/C14", via 07ac55a1c, with a saturation test
# (lib.rs:2955-3068 per fenix's lane C); (9, wrapper half) the two thin
# main.rs wrappers were already closed in the fix-aw-readiness-easy rounds
# below (f3345fa70).
#
# Genuinely STILL OPEN, no fix landed, no deferral recorded -- disclosed to
# fenix/team-lead in the qa-phase-aw-integration-review-r2 verdict, requires
# a fix dispatch or an explicit deferral-with-owner before full closure:
# (4) dev/prod allowed_dependencies conflation, boundaries/atm-http-runtime/
# http-runtime.toml:30,53 (documented as a known gap, not structurally
# split -- proposed fix: an allowed_dev_dependencies key); (5) untyped
# loopback_tcp_get_json GET-any-path escape hatch,
# crates/atm-http-runtime/src/client.rs:191 (no boundary lint rule catches
# it); (6) internal constant re-exported as public API -- not independently
# re-verified this round; (7) DiagnosticTimeline::prune has no production
# caller, crates/atm-storage/src/diagnostics.rs:137 (wire into retention or
# delete); (9, unused-field half) stale RuntimeHealth doc/plan claim -- not
# independently re-verified this round; (10) oversized atm-observability/
# sc-observability/tracing-subscriber edge pulled into the Python wheel to
# consume two constants -- not independently re-verified this round; missing
# ADR for the retained-diagnostics pipeline -- not independently re-verified
# this round. Bundle remains "open" at the finding level pending these. The
# occurrence below (item 4, the sharpest of the remaining gaps -- it masks
# the exact prod edge AW.3 was meant to keep closed) is added as a new
# hasOccurrence-linked branch occurrence so the branch-scoped live-count gate
# correctly continues to report this finding as open pending a fix or an
# explicit Rand-approved deferral.
